    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the manual says it's a leak protection issue. how do i actually check the sensors in the bottom of the unit? i dont want to just call someone yet if i can dry it out myself.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since the manual mentions leak protection, the sensor is likely related to a flood detection system. You should carefully pull out the lower rack and inspect the area around the pump and sump basin for standing water; this indicates where the leak protection sensor might be triggered. If you see water, carefully wipe it dry, ensuring the sensor itself is clean and dry before attempting another cycle. Be cautious and only touch components you are comfortable with, as water and electricity are involved.",
